{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/34774-trading-up-on-cultists","id":34774,"title":"Trading up on Cultists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-21T21:26:42-08:00","id":34774,"title":"Trading up on Cultists","content":"I like to believe that the mummies care about their cult. The cult is the mummies arms and legs in the real world. They're an essential part of survival for the arisen. But I know this probably isn't very common. The mummy is a literal god to their cultists, whose very being inspires awe and fear into those that see the dead sorcerer.<br /> <br /> My question is, would a mummy trade cultists with other mummies?<br /> <br /> A mummy treats their cultists as pawns in their chess game. If they can garner favors or rewards for a valuable cultist, why wouldn't the arisen try and move their pawn to the other side of the board. Of course cultists aren't baseball players, and trading them around would be pretty dickish. BUT! What if you convinced them that it was their divine mission. An enterprising Maa-Kep might use their cultists as spies on other mummies. The alchemists probably wouldn't have a problem, their goal is to gather dedwen and gathering valuable cultists might be a good way to do that.<br /> <br /> So yeah, is it viable for a mummy to trade their cultists? Or would it just be too risky?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T11:42:50-08:00","id":35700,"title":"","content":"It sounds about as risky as employing spies would be for anybody. That doesn't stop agencies from doing so.<br /> <br /> Tribal cultists might be very loyal but enterprise and conspiracy cultists might even betray you if the price is right","signature":"","edited":{"userid":638,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","user":"reseru","date":".  added more stuff 12-23-2013, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}